theory.intro:
The **average rate of change** of $y = f(x)$ over $[a, b]$, where $a < b$, is how much $y$ changes per unit of $x$ on average. It is the gradient of the **secant**, the straight line through $(a, f(a))$ and $(b, f(b))$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.3:5.0,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.18*\x*\x + 0.4}) node[above left] {$y=f(x)$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (1.2,0.6592) -- (4.3,0.6592) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$\Delta x$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (4.3,0.6592) -- (4.3,3.7282) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$\Delta y$};
\draw[thick,red] (0.8,0.2632) -- (4.8,4.2232) node[right,font=\small] {secant};
\fill (1.2,0.6592) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (4.3,3.7282) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\small] at (1.2,0.6592) {$(a,f(a))$};
\node[above left,font=\small] at (4.3,3.7282) {$(b,f(b))$};
\draw (1.2,0) -- (1.2,-0.12) node[below] {$a$};
\draw (4.3,0) -- (4.3,-0.12) node[below] {$b$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
The graph of $y=f(x)$ contains $A(-3,9)$ and $B(2,-1)$. Find the average rate of change over $[-3,2]$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.35cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (-4,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-3)--(0,11) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=-3.4:2.4,samples=60] plot (\x,{0.2*\x*\x-1.8*\x+1.8});
\fill[black] (-3,9) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$A(-3,9)$};
\fill[black] (2,-1) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$B(2,-1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Join $A$ and $B$ with a secant. Moving from $A$ to $B$, the horizontal change is $5$ and the vertical change is $-10$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.35cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{secantRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,black] (-4,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-3)--(0,11) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveBlue,domain=-3.4:2.4,samples=60] plot (\x,{0.2*\x*\x-1.8*\x+1.8});
\draw[thick,secantRed] (-3.4,9.8)--(2.4,-1.8);
\draw[dashed,black] (-3,9)--(2,9) node[midway,above] {$\Delta x=5$};
\draw[dashed,black] (2,9)--(2,-1) node[midway,right] {$\Delta y=-10$};
\fill[black] (-3,9) circle (2pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill[black] (2,-1) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}\text{Average rate}&=\frac{f(2)-f(-3)}{2-(-3)}\\&=\frac{-1-9}{5}\\&=-2\end{aligned}$

